# L §7.6 item 1 (tally 2.1.6, issue #89): a day computed past 9999-12-31 or before 0001-01-01 is refused at its
# key, RUN-LIMIT, and so is the end of time where a day is read: printed (end_of(9999)), a day argument (year_of,
# weekday), a balance's day. The edges stand: 9999-12-31 itself, 0001-01-02 - 1 day, end_of(9999) - 1 day. tally
# 2.1.5's refcore refused the model REFCORE-NOT-YET (its run lies in 9999).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 9999-12-31
  start 9999-01-01
  end 9999-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place other: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input d: date
input amt: money PLN

version v
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 9999-01-01
  d = 9999-12-31 "plan"
  amt = 100.00 PLN "plan"
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 9999-01-01 start "plan"

ask last: d
ask past: d + 1 day
ask past2: end_of(9999-12) + 1 day
ask month: add_months(9999-12-15, 1)
ask eot: end_of(9999)
ask year: year_of(end_of(9999))
ask wd: weekday(end_of(9999-12))
ask bal: bal(konto, end_of(9999))
ask first: 0001-01-02 - 1 day
ask before: 0001-01-01 - 1 day
ask back: end_of(9999) - 1 day
=== expect
back: 9999-12-31
  cut 9999-12-31
bal: refused: RUN-LIMIT a day passes 9999-12-31
  cut 9999-12-31
before: refused: RUN-LIMIT a day comes before 0001-01-01
  cut 9999-12-31
eot: refused: RUN-LIMIT a day passes 9999-12-31
first: 0001-01-01
  cut 9999-12-31
last: 9999-12-31
  cut 9999-12-31
month: refused: RUN-LIMIT a day passes 9999-12-31
  cut 9999-12-31
past: refused: RUN-LIMIT a day passes 9999-12-31
  cut 9999-12-31
past2: refused: RUN-LIMIT a day passes 9999-12-31
  cut 9999-12-31
wd: refused: RUN-LIMIT a day passes 9999-12-31
  cut 9999-12-31
year: refused: RUN-LIMIT a day passes 9999-12-31
  cut 9999-12-31
warning: WARN-UNREAD input amt is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD place landlord is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD place other is read by nothing
